al constraint has opened a completely different line of investigation: I am checking if there is a sequence in the output, since the 5's are acting like an important signal.\n\n\n**Tracing Column-Wise Outputs**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on the outputs column by column. The pattern is clear: alternating 3s and 5s! But the starting value of each column alternates across the training data: it is either 3 or 5! It seems the starting value depends on the row position of the initial '5' in each column. I am trying to formalize how to determine the initial value.\n\n\n**Determining Output Initialization**\n\nI've hit on something big! Analyzing the training data, I've realized that the length of the column's sequence determines its starting value. Odd-length columns begin with '3', while even-length columns start with '5'. Furthermore, the end always resolves to '3'! I'm now formalizing this and building the rules, connecting them to the width. I'm excited!\n\n\n",
